WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
- Hi, I'm Rie.

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.150
I'm a Tasty producer.

00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:05.710
Today, I'm making a
dish without any trash.

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:08.050
I don't know what is the dish yet.

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:11.023
It's gonna be a surprise,
and I don't like surprise.

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:14.010
You know, in a daily
life when you're cooking,

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:16.310
you're making a lot of
trash without noticing.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:19.810
In the kitchen, I use
a lot of saran wraps,

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:21.393
plastic containers.

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:24.300
I feel like I should be
more conscious about it.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:27.593
We make a lot of trash,
and where does it go?

00:00:33.614 --> 00:00:34.614
What's this?

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:35.623
Apple pie?

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:38.933
Apple has cores and stem.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:40.230
So, apple pie.

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:44.003
We will need flour, butter, apples,

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:45.593
cinnamon powder, and sugar.

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:48.460
Most of the dry ingredients
come in a package,

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:51.290
so I hope we can find a grocery store

00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:54.952
that has bulk section so I
can bring my own containers.

00:00:54.952 --> 00:00:58.233
(laughs) This look like
potato, let's do potato pie.

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:03.220
So, this was my first time
going to the grocery store

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:04.743
with bulk section.

00:01:29.981 --> 00:01:32.063
Less trash is still trash.

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:33.457
Trash, trash (laughs).

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:37.713
And we got little bit
cinnamon in a giant jar.

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:40.503
I've got Granny Smith apples.

00:01:46.018 --> 00:01:48.435
It has sticker on it, so sad.

00:01:48.530 --> 00:01:51.830
I just remembered I made this

00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:54.453
beautiful rose apple pie for Tasty,

00:01:54.490 --> 00:01:56.810
and I can use apple skin.

00:01:56.810 --> 00:01:59.380
That's kind of bummer
because I chose green apple.

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:01.313
I should have chose red apple.

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:03.163
That's why I don't like surprises.

00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:07.100
I'm still figuring out how to use core.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:09.163
Maybe I'm gonna just eat them.

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:12.157
I'll sacrifice myself for
this challenge (laughs).

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:15.603
Making pie.

00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:17.370
Now, we're gonna make a pie crust.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:20.010
Alright, quarter cup of sugar,

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:24.113
two and a quarter cup of
flour, and now butter.

00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:27.933
You wanna use cold butter
and cut into small pieces.

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:31.850
This is the butter with least
amount of trash we could find.

00:02:31.850 --> 00:02:33.220
Trash in a bowl.

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:35.330
Okay, I'm gonna use this bowl scraper

00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:37.800
to make butter small pieces.

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:42.800
Okay, and now I'm adding the
ice water in a pie dough.

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:44.880
I love making pie.

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:47.523
It's something very calming about it.

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:51.283
My pie dough is almost done, and usually,

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:54.403
you have to wrap with saran wrap.

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:56.410
Saran wrap is also waste,

00:02:56.410 --> 00:02:59.440
so I think if I have a container with lid,

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:01.143
it's gonna totally do the job.

00:03:05.123 --> 00:03:06.473
I'm gonna wash my hands.

00:03:08.543 --> 00:03:11.210
(water running)

00:03:12.751 --> 00:03:14.333
Peeling the stickers.

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:16.383
It's kind of sad.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:22.680
After that, I'm gonna wash this
apple and slice them thinly.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.053
Struggles.

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:33.643
I'm gonna make a separate waste,
like food waste and trash.

00:03:35.690 --> 00:03:37.623
But you know, the taste will be good.

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:38.613
Very tart.

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:40.173
This apple is very slippery.

00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:44.743
The rose apple pie I
made was without peel.

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:47.093
So, what if it doesn't work?

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:51.093
I'm going to macerate with sugar.

00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:54.580
Half cup of sugar, half
cup of brown sugar,

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:55.633
but we don't have it.

00:03:56.361 --> 00:03:57.194
Cinnamon.

00:03:58.060 --> 00:04:00.740
Okay, and leave this another 30 minutes

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:02.693
so it's gonna get soft.

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:09.000
Alright, so my pie dough
is chilled for 30 minute,

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:11.803
and I'm going to roll out this dough.

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:14.643
Sprinkle flour on the surface.

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:20.257
I think it's a good size.

00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:27.590
So, I'm going to prick...

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:29.543
Do you say prick?

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:32.370
Prick the dough so it doesn't puff up.

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:35.303
We have this apple macerated.

00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:45.270
I have leftover juice, and
I'm going to boil it down,

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:47.763
make a syrup, and I can top with that.

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:53.123
It's not that much, and
I'm gonna grab a spatula.

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:58.893
Oh, no, if it burned...

00:04:59.797 --> 00:05:00.630
Oh, okay.

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:03.383
No waste.

00:05:04.408 --> 00:05:06.741
(crunching)

00:05:09.183 --> 00:05:11.090
Okay, so I have a leftover dough.

00:05:11.090 --> 00:05:13.443
What kind of pattern should I make?

00:05:13.730 --> 00:05:14.983
Leaf, maybe?

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:20.580
Usually, you stick with egg wash.

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:24.887
You know, if I use egg, there
will be egg shell, egg carton,

00:05:24.887 --> 00:05:28.723
so I'm gonna just put water
and hope for the best.

00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:32.470
I feel pretty good about
the amount of waste I made.

00:05:32.470 --> 00:05:34.000
I don't wanna speak too soon.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.123
So, I have some leftover dough.

00:05:36.220 --> 00:05:40.493
What about if I make pie, pie.

00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:42.943
I use all dough, yay!

00:05:43.060 --> 00:05:48.060
So, I got this silicon mat you
can use as a parchment paper.

00:05:48.754 --> 00:05:49.713
Pie.

00:05:50.920 --> 00:05:53.453
So, I'm gonna go bake in the oven.

00:05:53.668 --> 00:05:54.501
Bye!

00:05:58.697 --> 00:05:59.530
40 minute.

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:03.083
Ta da!

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:04.013
Pie.

00:06:04.270 --> 00:06:05.730
I think I did great.

00:06:05.730 --> 00:06:08.570
It was hard, but it's totally doable.

00:06:08.570 --> 00:06:11.963
When I started, I was 50% confident,

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:14.343
but I made this beautiful pie

00:06:14.343 --> 00:06:17.060
and I'm pretty feel good about it,

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:20.527
both my pie and the
amount of trash I created.

00:06:20.527 --> 00:06:22.420
So, I think we should be more conscious

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:25.710
about how much trash we
are making in daily life.

00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:28.480
If you are more conscious
about what you choose,

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:30.780
you can totally make less waste.

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:33.500
So, I'm going to share
this with my coworkers,

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:35.333
and let's see what they think.

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:37.183
- Wow!

00:06:37.183 --> 00:06:38.623
- Those look like sausages.

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:39.580
- It looks pretty!

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:43.060
- I had to make this pie
without making any waste,

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:46.183
and this is the amount of trash I created.

00:06:46.657 --> 00:06:48.013
- Oh!
- Nice.

00:06:48.013 --> 00:06:49.046
(all talking)

00:06:49.046 --> 00:06:50.177
- And you folded it?

00:06:50.177 --> 00:06:51.927
- You could eat that.

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:55.033
- I can compost the core after I eat it.

00:06:55.910 --> 00:06:57.493
- Do we eat?
- Yeah, please.

00:06:58.243 --> 00:06:59.915
(laughing)

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:00.833
- Fantastic.

00:07:01.160 --> 00:07:02.470
- Also, doesn't it taste better

00:07:02.470 --> 00:07:04.550
knowing that hardly any trash was created?

00:07:04.550 --> 00:07:05.700
I'm actually really impressed

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:08.470
because I have not tried to
make something this ambitious,

00:07:08.470 --> 00:07:09.730
but you've inspired me.

00:07:09.730 --> 00:07:10.630
- This is so good.

00:07:10.840 --> 00:07:13.563
- Simple, tasty, delicious.

00:07:14.397 --> 00:07:16.049
- Tasty, no wastey.

00:07:16.049 --> 00:07:18.351
- [Nikki] There's nothing else to say.

00:07:18.351 --> 00:07:22.320
Tasty, no wastey.
(laughing)

